<title>USA: CII Technologies cuts estimated IPO range.</title>
<headline>CII Technologies cuts estimated IPO range.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>CII Technologies Inc has cut the terms of its estimated pricing range to $7 to $9, according to documents filed with the U.S. Securities and Exhchange Commission on Monday.</p>
<p>Previously, the company planned to price shares in a range of $9 to $11. The offering is due sometime this week, according to lead underwriter William Blair.</p>
<p>CII plans to offer 3.5 million shares under the symbol &quot;CIIT&quot; on the Nasdaq. The Fairview, North Carolina company makes electromechanical and solid state relays and solenoids, used to control current or signals in electrical circuits.</p>
</text>
